  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The sources of packages/llama_engine/assets/models.json (the on-device AI models).",
    "tool/llm_catalog.py resolve turns them into it through Hugging Face's API: the commit of each revision, then the size and SHA-256 (LFS object id) of the file at that commit; the URL is pinned to the commit. Sizes and checksums are never written by hand.",
    "A model names one repo, revision and file, or several candidates tried in order (the first repo that exists, is not gated and has the file wins). When a repo names its files differently, the one .gguf of the model's quantization is picked; none or several is an error.",
    "revision: a branch (main) until the catalogue is resolved, then the commit it was resolved at.",
    "minRamMb / recommendedRamMb: RAM in MiB as Android reports it (ActivityManager totalMem, a little below the nominal size): below the minimum the model is not offered for download (importing it stays possible), below the recommendation the app says it may be slow.",
    "languages (translation models): the app's language codes (packages/translation_repository language catalogue)."
  ],
